# Fix the PR before you return

When a review, check, or your own read of a pull request finds a change that should be made, make it on that branch. Do not stop at a list of proposed fixes.

- Push the fixes to the open pull request. Do not open a second pull request for the same fix.
- Do not force-push. Do not commit secrets, `.env`, or Terraform state.

If the change has tests, or the pull request runs CI, stay until CI is green.

- Run the tests that cover the change.
- Watch the pull request checks. If one fails, read the log, fix the cause, and push again.
- Do not return while a required check is failing, pending, or not yet reported after a push you just made. Wait for the run to finish.
- A skipped test is not a pass. If a test was skipped because env was missing, say so only after the tests that can run are green. Do not hide a failure behind a skip.
